From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A7om <hatter6822@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hw/misc/bcm2835_property: Keep every tag within its value
 buffer

Each tag declares the size of its value buffer, and the firmware reads
the request's fields from that buffer and writes its answer into it.
Most handlers ignored the size: an eight-byte answer went into a
four-byte buffer, over the tag that followed, and a request field the
buffer did not hold was read from whatever came next. A guest that got
a size wrong saw its request corrupted rather than answered short, and
the parser then went on through what the handler had written.

Route every access through two helpers that stay inside the buffer: a
field beyond it reads as zero and is not written, while the response
length still says how much the whole answer needs, as the identity
tags already do. The palette and OTP tags, whose requests are lists,
take only the entries the buffer holds, and a palette request whose
entries are not all there is invalid. The command line keeps its
firmware-observed behaviour of copying nothing into a buffer too short
for it.
---
 hw/misc/bcm2835_property.c | 193 ++++++++++++++++++++++---------------
 1 file changed, 113 insertions(+), 80 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/misc/bcm2835_property.c b/hw/misc/bcm2835_property.c
index 362c1a7..d4d9a03 100644
--- a/hw/misc/bcm2835_property.c
+++ b/hw/misc/bcm2835_property.c
@@ -51,6 +51,30 @@ static size_t bcm2835_property_answer32(BCM2835PropertyState *s,
     return bcm2835_property_answer(s, value, bufsize, &le, sizeof(le));
 }
 
+/*
+ * One word of the tag's value buffer, @offset bytes into it. A request
+ * field the buffer does not hold reads as zero, and an answer it does not
+ * hold is not written; the response length still says how much the whole
+ * answer needs.
+ */
+static uint32_t bcm2835_property_get32(BCM2835PropertyState *s, hwaddr value,
+                                       uint32_t bufsize, uint32_t offset)
+{
+    if (offset + 4 > bufsize) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    return ldl_le_phys(&s->dma_as, value + 12 + offset);
+}
+
+static void bcm2835_property_put32(BCM2835PropertyState *s, hwaddr value,
+                                   uint32_t bufsize, uint32_t offset,
+                                   uint32_t data)
+{
+    if (offset + 4 <= bufsize) {
+        stl_le_phys(&s->dma_as, value + 12 + offset, data);
+    }
+}
